<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Detailed Derivations and Proof</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>ELBO Derivation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward chain.</span>
For any observation <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the forward diffusion constructs as</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})=\prod_{t=1}^{T}q_{t}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})=\prod_{t=1}^{T}q_{t}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">note we represent <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{z}}_{0}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{z}}_{0}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> since the transform <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reverse generative model.</span></p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T})=p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\;\Big[\prod_{t=2}^{T}p_{\theta}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\big)\Big]\;p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T})=p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\;\Big[\prod_{t=2}^{T}p_{\theta}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\big)\Big]\;p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(ELBO decomposition)<span id="Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the forward chain <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> defined in equation <a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation A.1 ‣ A.1 ELBO Derivation ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> and reverse model <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> in equation <a href="#A1.E2" title="Equation A.2 ‣ A.1 ELBO Derivation ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we have the decomposed ELBO as following:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})\big]}_{\text{reconstruction term at }t=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">reconstruction term at </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})\big]}_{\text{reconstruction term at }t=1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\underbrace{\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big\|\,p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big]}_{\text{denoising matches for }t&gt;1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">denoising matches for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\underbrace{\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big\|\,p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big]}_{\text{denoising matches for }t&gt;1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\|\,p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\big)}_{\text{prior match at }T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">prior match at </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\|\,p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\big)}_{\text{prior match at }T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})=p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})=p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the prior match term is zero. The bound is tight if and only if</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})=q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\quad\text{for all }t\geq 2," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})=q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\quad\text{for all }t\geq 2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the prior match is zero, and the decoder <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> equals the true conditional induced by the joint.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Recap the forward kernel defined in equation <a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 4.3 ‣ 4.1 Forward ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> and equation <a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4.4 ‣ 4.1 Forward ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1})=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathrm{Categorical}\big({\bm{x}}_{t}^{i};\ {\bm{Q}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}\big),\penalty\ \penalty\ \penalty\ {\bm{Q}}_{t}=(1-\beta_{t}){\bm{I}}+\beta_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\,\bm{m}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>Categorical</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1})=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathrm{Categorical}\big({\bm{x}}_{t}^{i};\ {\bm{Q}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}\big),\penalty\ \penalty\ \penalty\ {\bm{Q}}_{t}=(1-\beta_{t}){\bm{I}}+\beta_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\,\bm{m}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\begin{cases}\delta({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}-{\bm{z}}_{t-1}^{i}),&{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}},\\
\mathcal{N}\!\big({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i};\ \sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{t-1}^{i},\ (1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}}_{d}\big),&{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}},{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}},\\
\mathcal{N}\!\big({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i};\ \sqrt{\gamma_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{t-1}^{i},\ (1-\gamma_{t}){\bm{I}}_{d}\big),&{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}},{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}={\bm{m}}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\begin{cases}\delta({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}-{\bm{z}}_{t-1}^{i}),&amp;{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}},\\
\mathcal{N}\!\big({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i};\ \sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{t-1}^{i},\ (1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}}_{d}\big),&amp;{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}},{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}},\\
\mathcal{N}\!\big({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i};\ \sqrt{\gamma_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{t-1}^{i},\ (1-\gamma_{t}){\bm{I}}_{d}\big),&amp;{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}},{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}={\bm{m}}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3 (ELBO decomposition). ‣ A.1 ELBO Derivation ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is mostly done in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sohl-Dickstein et al. (2015)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al. (2020)</a></cite>. We include the following proof to show the generalized version with added variables. Start from the evidence identity and apply Jensen inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\int q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\frac{p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T})}{q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\;d{\bm{x}}_{1:T}\,d{\bm{z}}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\int q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\frac{p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T})}{q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\;d{\bm{x}}_{1:T}\,d{\bm{z}}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T})-\log q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T})-\log q({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=:{\mathcal{L}}(\theta;{\bm{x}}_{0})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=:{\mathcal{L}}(\theta;{\bm{x}}_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Insert the model and forward factorizations equation <a href="#A1.E2" title="Equation A.2 ‣ A.1 ELBO Derivation ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> and equation <a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation A.1 ‣ A.1 ELBO Derivation ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\theta;{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\theta;{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\Big[\log p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})+\sum_{t=2}^{T}\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\Big[\log p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})+\sum_{t=2}^{T}\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> use Bayes’ rule under <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\frac{q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\;q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}{q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\frac{q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\;q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}{q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q}[\log(\cdot)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q}[\log(\cdot)]</annotation></semantics></math> of equation <a href="#A1.E7" title="Equation A.7 ‣ Proof of Proposition . ‣ A.1 ELBO Derivation ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a> and rearranging gives, for <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\Big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})-\log q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\Big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})-\log q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=-\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=-\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\quad-\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]+\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\quad-\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]+\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Sum equation <a href="#A1.E8" title="Equation A.8 ‣ Proof of Proposition . ‣ A.1 ELBO Derivation ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a> over <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math>. The last two expectations telescope:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Plug this back into equation <a href="#A1.E6" title="Equation A.6 ‣ Proof of Proposition . ‣ A.1 ELBO Derivation ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a> and group the boundary terms with <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\theta;{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\theta;{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\Big(\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]-\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\big]\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\Big(\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]-\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\big]\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">Now we recoginize the prior KL to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\theta;{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\theta;{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{t=2}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\big)\;-\;\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]}_{=:C({\bm{x}}_{0})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\big)\;-\;\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\log q({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{z}}_{1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\big]}_{=:C({\bm{x}}_{0})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">Note the last term <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C({\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> does not involve <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and can be dropped, and we normally do not optimize the last KL term <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\ \|\ p_{T}({\bm{x}}_{T},{\bm{z}}_{T})\big)</annotation></semantics></math> as we let the schedule to make this statistical distance is sufficiently small.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Forward</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We can derive the following lemma for the marginal at time step <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Continuous marginal conditioned on <math id="Thmlemma2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Recap <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\gamma}_{t}:=\prod_{s=1}^{t}\gamma_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\gamma}_{t}:=\prod_{s=1}^{t}\gamma_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each position <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we have continuous marginal conditioned on <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i},{\bm{x}}_{0}^{i})=\begin{cases}\delta({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}-{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i}),&{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{x}}_{0}^{i},\\
\mathcal{N}\!\big({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i};\ \sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},\ (1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}}_{d}\big),&{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i},{\bm{x}}_{0}^{i})=\begin{cases}\delta({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}-{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i}),&amp;{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{x}}_{0}^{i},\\
\mathcal{N}\!\big({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i};\ \sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},\ (1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}}_{d}\big),&amp;{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i}={\bm{w}}_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i}={\bm{w}}_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence We finally have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{n}q({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i},{\bm{x}}_{0}^{i})=\Big[\!\!\!\prod_{i:\,{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}}}\!\!\!\delta({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}-{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i})\Big]\cdot\Big[\!\!\!\prod_{i:\,{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}}}\!\!\!\mathcal{N}({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i};\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}}_{d})\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{n}q({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i},{\bm{x}}_{0}^{i})=\Big[\!\!\!\prod_{i:\,{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}}}\!\!\!\delta({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}-{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i})\Big]\cdot\Big[\!\!\!\prod_{i:\,{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}}}\!\!\!\mathcal{N}({\bm{z}}_{t}^{i};\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}}_{d})\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then what follows proves Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We first prove the conditional independency between <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> in the reverse context.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional independency between <math id="Thmlemma3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="Thmlemma3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are conditionally independent given <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> based on the forward kerned defined in equation <a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4.4 ‣ 4.1 Forward ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To prove Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Timestep-𝑡 joint marginal factorization). ‣ 4.1 Forward ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we first prove the following lemma:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Continuous marginal conditioned on (𝒙_𝑡,𝒙_0)). ‣ A.2 Forward ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Conditional independency between 𝒛_𝑡 and 𝒙_{𝑡-1} given (𝒙_𝑡,𝒙_0)). ‣ A.2 Forward ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{x}}_{0}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{x}}_{0}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> then the absorbing chain implies <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{s}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{s}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq t</annotation></semantics></math>, so the kernel gives
<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{z}}_{0}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{z}}_{0}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely, which is the first line of equation <a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4.4 ‣ 4.1 Forward ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}^{i}={\bm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, use the law of total probability over <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}\in\{{\bm{x}}_{0}^{i},{\bm{m}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}\in\{{\bm{x}}_{0}^{i},{\bm{m}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}\neq{\bm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> (first time masking at <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>), the second branch of the kernel gives
<math id="A1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}={\bm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}^{i}={\bm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> (already masked), the third branch composes a diffusion forward step with the
previous marginal <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t-1}^{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}){\bm{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t-1}^{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}){\bm{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
which yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}\ \sim\ \mathcal{N}\!\big(\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},\ (1-\gamma_{t}\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}){\bm{I}}\big)=\mathcal{N}\!\big(\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},\ (1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t}^{i}\ \sim\ \mathcal{N}\!\big(\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},\ (1-\gamma_{t}\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}){\bm{I}}\big)=\mathcal{N}\!\big(\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{0}^{i},\ (1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}){\bm{I}}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the masked line of equation <a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4.4 ‣ 4.1 Forward ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Then leveraging these results, we can easily prove Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Timestep-𝑡 joint marginal factorization). ‣ 4.1 Forward ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Timestep-𝑡 joint marginal factorization). ‣ 4.1 Forward ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expand the path marginal, use equation <a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 4.2 ‣ 4.1 Forward ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Continuous marginal conditioned on (𝒙_𝑡,𝒙_0)). ‣ A.2 Forward ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, and factor over positions.
The sum over discrete paths yields <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>; conditioning on <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces the continuous part to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Continuous marginal conditioned on (𝒙_𝑡,𝒙_0)). ‣ A.2 Forward ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Reverse</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first prove the factorization shown in equation <a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 4.10 ‣ Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>. To achieve this, we just need to show:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\cdot q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\cdot q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})}{q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})}\cdot q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})}{q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})}\cdot q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\cdot q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\cdot q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})=q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})=q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> by the conditional independence according to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Conditional independency between 𝒛_𝑡 and 𝒙_{𝑡-1} given (𝒙_𝑡,𝒙_0)). ‣ A.2 Forward ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Then the discrete part is the same as discrete diffusion, we may leverage the results from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al. (2021a)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al. (2024)</a></cite> to complete the proof of equation <a href="#S4.E11" title="Equation 4.11 ‣ Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we prove the closed form of the continuous part, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},\mathbf{z}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},\mathbf{z}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, by case analysis based on the discrete states. We start with Bayes’ rule for the continuous variables:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})\propto q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t})\cdot q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})\propto q({\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{t})\cdot q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The forms of the two terms on the right-hand side are Gaussian distributions, but will change depending on the discrete states and it leads to the three cases.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1: No mask at <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}={\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}={\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>).<span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> In this case, no noise has been applied to the embedding up to timestep t-1. Thus, both terms directly have a Dirac delta function: <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1}={\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\delta({\bm{z}}_{t-1}-{\bm{z}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1}={\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\delta({\bm{z}}_{t-1}-{\bm{z}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. The posterior is therefore also a Dirac delta function, proving the first part of equation <a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 4.12 ‣ Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2: First time unmask at <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}={\bm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}={\bm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}={\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}={\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>).<span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> In this case, the first term in equation <a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation A.15 ‣ Proof of Proposition . ‣ A.3 Reverse ‣ Appendix A Detailed Derivations and Proof ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.15</span></a> is Gaussian while the second term becomes a Dirac <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta({\bm{z}}_{t-1}-{\bm{z}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta({\bm{z}}_{t-1}-{\bm{z}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. The multiplication yields a Dirac posterior at the same point: <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1}={\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\delta({\bm{z}}_{t-1}-{\bm{z}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1}={\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{0})=\delta({\bm{z}}_{t-1}-{\bm{z}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 3: Remaining masked at <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}={\bm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}={\bm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}={\bm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}={\bm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>).<span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> In this case, both terms remain in Gaussian distribution, and the parameters are same with normal Gaussian diffusion models. The product of these two Gaussians is a new Gaussian, allowing us to use the standard derivation for DDPM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, by completing the square on the exponent, we find that the resulting distribution is <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z}_{t-1};\,\tilde{\bm{{\bm{\mu}}}}_{t}(\mathbf{z}_{t},\mathbf{z}_{0}),\ \tilde{\beta}_{t}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z}_{t-1};\,\tilde{\bm{{\bm{\mu}}}}_{t}(\mathbf{z}_{t},\mathbf{z}_{0}),\ \tilde{\beta}_{t}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, which proves the last part of equation <a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 4.12 ‣ Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the results from Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, for a single position <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the exact one–step KL at timestep <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> inside the ELBO is</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}({\bm{x}}_{0},t):=\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big\|\,p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}({\bm{x}}_{0},t):=\mathbb{E}_{q({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})}\!\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big\|\,p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)\Big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the unmasked positions (<math id="A1.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}\neq{\bm{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}\neq{\bm{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>), the KL is identically <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and plug in equation <a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 4.10 ‣ Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>, <a href="#S4.E11" title="Equation 4.11 ‣ Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a> and <a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 4.12 ‣ Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>, we recover equation <a href="#S4.E14" title="Equation 4.14 ‣ Lemma 1. ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.14</span></a> exactly as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)=\underbrace{\rho_{t}^{\mathrm{flip}}\ \big[-\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}|{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big]}_{\text{discrete}}+\underbrace{\rho_{t}^{\mathrm{keep}}\ \mathcal{D_{\mathrm{KL}}}^{\mathrm{cont}}}_{\text{continuous}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>flip</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>discrete</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>keep</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>cont</mi></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>continuous</mtext></munder><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(q(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big)=\underbrace{\rho_{t}^{\mathrm{flip}}\ \big[-\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}|{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t})\big]}_{\text{discrete}}+\underbrace{\rho_{t}^{\mathrm{keep}}\ \mathcal{D_{\mathrm{KL}}}^{\mathrm{cont}}}_{\text{continuous}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">with the ratio that determines whether the position is going to be flipped to unmask:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}^{\mathrm{keep}}=\frac{1-\alpha_{t-1}}{1-\alpha_{t}},\qquad\rho_{t}^{\mathrm{flip}}=\frac{\alpha_{t-1}\,\beta_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}=\frac{\alpha_{t-1}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>keep</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>flip</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}^{\mathrm{keep}}=\frac{1-\alpha_{t-1}}{1-\alpha_{t}},\qquad\rho_{t}^{\mathrm{flip}}=\frac{\alpha_{t-1}\,\beta_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}=\frac{\alpha_{t-1}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">The discrete KL part exactly recovers the results from the absorbing discrete diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al., 2021a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and the continuous KL divergence:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{cont}}=D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\Big(\mathcal{N}({\bm{\mu}}^{\star},\tilde{\beta}_{t}{\bm{I}}_{d})\ \Big\|\ \mathcal{N}({\bm{\mu}}_{v},\tilde{\beta}_{t}{\bm{I}}_{d})\Big),\quad{\bm{\mu}}^{\star}=\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}({\bm{z}}_{0},{\bm{z}}_{t}),\ \ {\bm{\mu}}_{v}=\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\hat{\bm{z}}_{0},{\bm{z}}_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>cont</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.667em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{cont}}=D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\Big(\mathcal{N}({\bm{\mu}}^{\star},\tilde{\beta}_{t}{\bm{I}}_{d})\ \Big\|\ \mathcal{N}({\bm{\mu}}_{v},\tilde{\beta}_{t}{\bm{I}}_{d})\Big),\quad{\bm{\mu}}^{\star}=\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}({\bm{z}}_{0},{\bm{z}}_{t}),\ \ {\bm{\mu}}_{v}=\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\hat{\bm{z}}_{0},{\bm{z}}_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">where we recap</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\\
\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\zeta,{\bm{z}}_{t})=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}}(1-\gamma_{t})}{1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,\zeta+\frac{\sqrt{\gamma_{t}}(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t-1})}{1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{t},\qquad\tilde{\beta}_{t}=\frac{(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t-1})(1-\gamma_{t})}{1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\
\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\zeta,{\bm{z}}_{t})=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}}(1-\gamma_{t})}{1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,\zeta+\frac{\sqrt{\gamma_{t}}(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t-1})}{1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}}\,{\bm{z}}_{t},\qquad\tilde{\beta}_{t}=\frac{(1-\bar{\gamma}_{t-1})(1-\gamma_{t})}{1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">This results in the comparison between <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{z}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{z}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the KL divergence reduced to:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{cont}}=\frac{1}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}}\,\big\|\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}({\bm{z}}_{0},{\bm{z}}_{t})-\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\hat{\bm{z}}_{0,\theta},{\bm{z}}_{t}^{i})\big\|^{2}=\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}}\;\|{\bm{z}}_{0}-\hat{\bm{z}}_{0,\theta}\|^{2};\ a_{t}=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}}(1-\gamma_{t})}{1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>cont</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{cont}}=\frac{1}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}}\,\big\|\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}({\bm{z}}_{0},{\bm{z}}_{t})-\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\hat{\bm{z}}_{0,\theta},{\bm{z}}_{t}^{i})\big\|^{2}=\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}}\;\|{\bm{z}}_{0}-\hat{\bm{z}}_{0,\theta}\|^{2};\ a_{t}=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\gamma}_{t-1}}(1-\gamma_{t})}{1-\bar{\gamma}_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(On the Alternative Factorization)<span id="Thmremark1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">One could also decompose the posterior using the alternative order from the chain rule:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid\cdot)=q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\cdot q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{t-1},{\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid\cdot)=q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\cdot q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\bm{x}}_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">While mathematically valid and could provide new properties in the sampling, this factorization is not fully tractable. The first term, <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}|\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{z}}_{t-1}|\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, is a complex Gaussian Mixture Model. More critically, the second term, <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}|\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}|\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, has no analytical closed form, as it would require inverting the continuous diffusion process and the embedding function to infer a discrete state. The factorization in Prop. <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is therefore adopted as a tractable choice for a more efficient algorithm implementation.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Detailed Experiment Settings</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Diffusion Settings</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The CADD forward process has two coupled components, each with its own schedule.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Discrete schedule: we adopt the MDLM log-linear masking schedule for the discrete process <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. The discrete forward corruption uses a continuous-time <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(t)=1-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(t)=1-t</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Continuous schedule: to keep the meaning of time aligned, we set the continuous latent <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> to follow a linear flow-matching path to isotropic noise <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lipman et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, i.e., if the position is masked, we have <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t}=(1-t){\bm{z}}_{0}+t{\bm{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t}=(1-t){\bm{z}}_{0}+t{\bm{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\epsilon}}\sim\mathcal{N}({\bm{0}},{\bm{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\epsilon}}\sim\mathcal{N}({\bm{0}},{\bm{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multi-sample estimation: we by default set <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math> for the estimation of <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{0,\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{0,\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> for fair comparison with the baselines. We provide ablation studies to demonstrate the effect of <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Experiment-Specific Settings</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Text Generation</span>
In our main experiments, including ablation studies that used to explore the properties of CADD, we train the models on OpenWebText. Following the standard MDLM pre-processing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, we use the GPT-2 tokenizer, resulting in a vocabulary of 50,257 tokens. The sequence length is fixed at 1,024. Our text model is a 12-layer DiT with 12 attention heads and an embedding dimension of 768, totaling approximately 168M parameters. During training, we keep the same training configuration, i.e., we train for about 2M steps with a batch size of 256 to match the total 262B tokens seen in the training. We use the AdamW optimizer with a learning rate warmed up from 0 to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. The results in Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ C.2 Perplexity Evaluation ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiment Results ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ C.2 Perplexity Evaluation ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiment Results ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, are based on Text8 and LM1B dataset, where we strictly follow the training setting in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jo &amp; Hwang (2024)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024)</a></cite>. Please refer their experiment settings for more details. For evaluation, we follow ReMDM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>’s evaluation setting, where we randomly sample 5,000 text samples with length <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1,024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1,024</annotation></semantics></math>, using <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{128,256,512,1024,4096\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>128,256,512</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1024</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4096</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{128,256,512,1024,4096\}</annotation></semantics></math> sampling steps. The sampled token sequences are used to compute MAUVE score, generative perplexity with GPT2-Large model, and entropy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Image Generation</span>
We experiment on CIFAR-10 and ImageNet (with resolution <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math>), which consists of 50,000 and 1,281,149 natural images respectively. CIFAR-10 already has <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math> resolution. For ImageNet images, we follow the preprocessing used in EDM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, i.e., using center-crop to make it a squared image and rescale to the desired <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math> resolution. As the model is trained on pixel space, we treat each pixel as a discrete token, resulting in a vocabulary size 256 at each position. We follow the architecture design used in MDM-Prime <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which is a U-Net architecture based on ADM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dhariwal &amp; Nichol, 2021</a>)</cite>. For CIFAR-10, we leverage an augmentation pipeline proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al. (2020)</a></cite>, but only keep the rotation and flip operation to avoid pixel value changes. We set the augmentation probability as 15% on CIFAR-10, and there is no augmentation used on ImageNet. For both experiments, we set learning rate as <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> using AdamW optimizer, and train the model until it has seen 200M and 4B images respectively. In sampling, we adopt a cosine decay for temperature with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{max}=2.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{max}=2.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and applied the corrector following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gat et al. (2024)</a></cite>. We use the standard Fréchet Inception Distance (FID) and Inception Score for evaluation, computed with 50,000 randomly generated images.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Code Generation</span>
We use the OpenCoder dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, selected by following the recipe in DiffuCoder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gong et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>. We strictly follow their settings to initialize the 7B model with Qwen2.5-Coder checkpoint, and adapt it to diffusion model using the techniques introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gong et al. (2025a)</a></cite>. Then we trained the model on 64 NVIDIA A100 GPUs in total. The training process utilized BF16 mixed precision and was scaled using Fully Sharded Data Parallelism (FSDP). For optimization, we employed the Adam optimizer with a peak learning rate of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, preceded by a 2,000-step linear warmup. The model is trained with 65B tokens in total. For generation, both models were configured with a maximum sequence length of 512 tokens and a total of T=512 diffusion timesteps. During generation, we employed a top negative entropy remasking sampler. The CADD from scratch variant uses temperature 0.2 and the DiffuCoder initialized variant uses temperature 0.01.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Experiment Results</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Training from mask diffusion model</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the experiments on code generation, we have seen CADD could be used to finentune an existing discrete (masking) diffusion model to improve the performance. Here we provide complementary evidence that such observation is also valid on text generation. We finetune a MDLM checkpoint with CADD objective for additional 50B tokens and evaluate the performance with same setting shown in the main experiments (Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Evaluation. ‣ 5.1 Text Generation ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). The results are shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ C.1 Training from mask diffusion model ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiment Results ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. The red curve shows close performance to the green one that represent CADD’s performance, which indicates CADD could efficiently finetune an existing MDM model to enhance the generation capabilities.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F5.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01329v1/mauve_vs_T_ft.svg" id="A3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/197;" width="476" height="197"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F5.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01329v1/genppl_vs_T_ft.svg" id="A3.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/197;" width="476" height="197"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A3.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Analogous figure of Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Evaluation. ‣ 5.1 Text Generation ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. We compare the finetuned checkpoint using CADD objective with CADD and the initialization checkpoint of MDLM. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Perplexity Evaluation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the objective of CADD involves the KL divergence of both discrete and continuous component as shown in equation <a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 4.10 ‣ Proposition 2 (Factorization of the true posterior). ‣ 4.2 Reverse ‣ 4 Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion (CADD) ‣ Continuously Augmented Discrete Diffusion model for Categorical Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>, it is not fair to compare the tightness of the bound directly with other models, and we choose to focus more on the evaluation of the generated samples. However, our model is still able to compute the likelihood of the discrete part. Here we put the results for reference, aiming to provide more information to help the readers understand how the model helps the discrete diffusion side.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure ltx_flex_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.T5.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.T5.fig1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A3.T5.fig1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Bits Per Character (BPC) results on Text8 test set. Results are taken from  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jo &amp; Hwang (2024)</a></cite>.
Bold denotes the best result in autoregressive or diffusion models. The best diffusion results are marked in bold.
</span></figcaption>
<div id="A3.T5.fig1.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:132.5pt;height:168.4pt;vertical-align:-81.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-5.5pt,7.0pt) scale(0.923020078760332,0.923020078760332) ;">
<table id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.4pt;padding-bottom:-0.4pt;">Method</td>
<td id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.4pt;padding-bottom:-0.4pt;">BPC (<math id="A3.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.4pt;padding-bottom:-0.4pt;"><span id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Autoregressive</span></td>
<td id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.4pt;padding-bottom:-0.4pt;"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:-0.4pt;padding-bottom:-0.4pt;">AR</td>
<td id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.4pt;padding-bottom:-0.4pt;"><span id="A3.T5.fig1.3.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.23</span></td></tr>
